{#-
  The proposal: the list of functional points the client reads and agrees to.

  It is the only document the analyst produces that somebody outside ever sees, and
  everything about it follows from that. It is written in the client's language — the
  one the pre-specification's front matter carries, never one guessed from the text —
  and the fixed words in it come from the language catalogues, which is where every
  text a person reads lives. There is none written here.

  The points are a table and not a paragraph: each row carries the identifier the
  system knows the point by, so that a point can be named without counting rows. The
  client validates the analysis point by point, and the demo is later accepted or
  refused against this same list.

  The texts of the points are a model's words, so they go through `cell`, which keeps
  one point on one row. Nothing written by a model is ever put in the front matter.

  This comment's tags carry the minus sign that strips the whitespace around them, so
  the rendered file begins with the front matter's first dash. A document whose first
  line is anything else has no front matter as far as workspaces is concerned.
-#}
---
project_id: {{ project_id }}
kind: proposal
template: {{ template }}
language: {{ language }}
---
# {{ title }}

{{ intro }}

| | |
|---|---|
{% for point in points %}
| {{ point.id }} | {{ point.text | cell }} |
{% endfor %}
